    "body": "<p>This Signature planner is a design tool for arranging virtual voices without masking. The user enters a list of virtual singers with preferred frequency bands and active time slots, and the planner reports every band-time cell where two or more singers overlap, scores the plan by total overlap, and suggests moves, shifting a singer&#x27;s band or slot, that reduce the score. The planner is the practical form of the acoustic niche hypothesis: it turns a descriptive idea about real habitats into a constructive tool for composers, game designers, and teachers. Every singer is invented, every parameter is stated, and every output is labelled a Signature design. This record covers all three layers, because a plan is only complete when geophony and anthrophony bands are entered alongside biophony.</p><h4>Science proof</h4><p>Science proof: the planner implements the niche principle that overlapping signals in the same band and time mask one another, a physical fact of hearing, and the design response, separation by band or time, that real communities exhibit. The planner does not claim that real species plan their niches; it claims only that separation reduces masking, which is measurable in its own overlap score.</p><h4>Math proof</h4><p>Math proof: if 5 singers occupy 5 distinct bands, overlap is 0 cells. If 2 singers share one band at the same time, overlap is 1 cell, and the overlap share over 5 band-time cells is 1 / 5 = 20.0 percent. The demo prints distinct-band overlap 0, shared-band overlap 1 cell, overlap share 20.0 percent, and the score after moving one singer to a free band, 0 cells.</p><h4>Soundscape layer(s)</h4><p>biophony; geophony; anthrophony</p><h4>Source</h4><p>Signature design study for this database, October 2026; acoustic niche hypothesis as in the public edition</p>",
